# amino: `t new -r amino "..."` from anywhere. Tests follow the repo's worktree-setup skill (path A):
# a postgres container of the worktree's own and bun test on the host, with no image build.
# TEARDOWN removes that container again, after every test run and before `t rm` deletes the worktree.
REPO=~/git/amino-monorepo
PIPELINE=amino-feature
TEST_CMD="$T_ROOT/repos/amino/run-tests"
TEARDOWN="$T_ROOT/repos/amino/teardown"
# +preview: ./dev.sh up with the app, backoffice and API each on a Cloudflare quick tunnel; TEARDOWN closes them
PREVIEW="$T_ROOT/repos/amino/preview"

# Generated by tooling, so no agent should read, edit or review them: they leave every diff, and
# every prompt says so. The migrations under backend/drizzle/*.sql are written by drizzle-kit too,
# but they are the schema change itself, so they stay in.
GENERATED="*openapi*.json *.gen.ts backend/drizzle/meta/* backend/src/db/migrate/id_mappings.json *bun.lock"
# implement runs it after the agent, so the API clients match the routes in every commit it makes
GENERATE="$T_ROOT/repos/amino/generate"
